title: "The ACS Project: Reasoning Substrate of Thinking Sands"
authors:
  - family-names: Esen
    given-names: Abdülhalim
repository-code: "https://github.com/LineBreaker30113/the-acs-project"
url: "https://github.com/LineBreaker30113/the-acs-project"
abstract: >-
  The Arity Component System (ACS) defines a novel database architecture
  implementing Polyadic Formal Concept Analysis (FCA)—a composable, multi-arity
  database substrate that formally models knowledge through atomic tables,
  invariant-preserving mathematical relations, and verifiable procedures. The ACS
  Project harnesses this database architecture as an experimental research
  testbed for high-reasoning Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) for reasoning
  LLMs. To explore how autonomous agents reason over evolving knowledge, the
  system introduces a live runtime class-loading mechanism that allows agents to
  safely synthesize, execute, and verify procedures while the database serves
  queries. The project formally investigates the fundamental trade-off between
  raw transaction latency and dynamic composability, serving as a formal
  laboratory for autonomous knowledge graph synthesis, request-level citation
  auditing, and lattice-based topological retrieval.
